  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Two billiard balls of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;each moving in opposite directions with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;collide and rebound with the same speed. If the time duration of contact is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>005</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, then what is the force exerted on the ball due to each other?"
  },
